MicroSensor Card Changes

Replace the pH/Gas MicroSensor Card
Replace the Chemistry MicroSensor Card
Monitor the hydration sequence after card installation

Cartridge and Reagent Changes

Replace the pH/Gas Calibrator Cartridge
Activate and replace the Chemistry Calibrator Cartridge (includes the 2-minute shake to activate)
Replace the Chemistry Reagent Cartridge (always changed with the Calibrator Cartridge)
Replace the CDV Bottle Pack and Reagent Cartridge (always changed together, triggers Adjust Intensity)
Replace the onboard Chemistry QC Cartridge (stored frozen, must be thawed before installation)
Replace the onboard pH/Gas QC Cartridge

Osmometer Maintenance

Change osmometer tubes (6 clean tubes + wash cup for Osm48, or tubes in positions 1–10 for Osm20)
Replace the wiper ring (Osm20 only)

Calibration

Initiate manual pH/Gas module calibration
Initiate manual Chemistry module calibration
Initiate combined pH/Gas and Chemistry calibration

Quality Control

Run onboard QC (select module and level, initiate analysis)
Run external QC (enter control ranges from product insert, then analyze)

Pump Tubing

Replace pH/Gas pump tubing harness
Replace Chemistry pump tubing harness

General

Log in and log out
Export results and logs to USB or shared folder
Respond to reagent status alerts (low volume, expired, empty)
Claim warranty credit when a MicroSensor Card parameter fails calibration three consecutive times
